# OTS project handoff

Full context lives in `AGENTS.md` (repo root). Human guide: `docs/GUIDE.md`. Read `AGENTS.md` first; this rule keeps only the hard constraints.

## Use Cases

- Any change to the public site, contact form, LinkedIn experience block, or production deploy.
- Picking up after a previous chat.

## Constraints

- Website only. No Tauri app, no `tools/ots-assistant/` here.
- Composer platform PHP `8.4.25` matches Hostinger; bump both together.
- Push to `master` deploys to production via `.github/workflows/deployToProduction.yml` → `deploy.sh`. `deploy.sh` stays tracked.
- Contact mail goes to `config('contact.admin_email')` only. No auto-reply. No `contact@` in HTML. No `otscommunity.com`.
- LinkedIn copy comes from the official export plus `config/linkedin.php` enrichments. No scraping, no Apify.
- Keep `fs-extra` devDependency and `npm` `overrides`.
- Never commit `.env`, `public/hot`, `.cursor/mcp.json`, `.mcp.json`. Never echo the MCP bearer token.
- Do not commit unless the user asks.

## Valid Examples

```php
Mail::to(config('contact.admin_email'))->queue(new ContactForAdminMail(...));
```

```bash
php artisan linkedin:sync-experience
```

## Invalid Examples

```php
Mail::to($request->input('email'))->send(...); // open relay
```

```bash
# Reintroducing Apify or scraping linkedin.com/in/... at request time
```
